<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="a9cabcb3-c257-593b-856b-3520f4c49ebb" activityNameId="41626185-05f3-5eac-816e-a45550eac67a" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Cable, ribbon cable, 20-pin, with plugs, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Cable, ribbon cable, 20-pin, with plugs, at plant
This dataset can be applied to describe the production of a typical 20-way ribbon cable to connect drives to the motherboard of a computer. The total weight of 1 unit of ribbon cable (with connector) is 0.0242 kg and the length 0.24 m, whereof the plugs weigh 0.0167 kg and the 20-cores cable 0.0075 kg. These weights have been extrapolated to 1 kg of ribbon cable (factor 1/0.0242). The information for this dataset is based on calculations and analyses at EMPA Laboratories. In 2023, only production efforts data are updated. Furthermore, material and energy input are now represented by global inventory flows; UUID: 62d03858-9356-3a2c-a739-8f5040b431f8
Describes the production of a typical ribbon cable with connectors for a desktop computer. Calculated per 1 kg of ribbon cable. Included are the materials copper, brass, PVC and HDPE with their attributed manufacturing processes like wire drawing or extrusion. The infrastructure is calculated via the proxy "electronic component production plant". Further inventoried are the electricity for the assembly of the connector, the fuel oil, propane and water input, the disposal of plastic and rubber parts, the VOC and methanol emissions created during the processing, plus the road and rail transportation for input materials from the regional storage to the production site. The accumulated hazardous waste is also reported.
Location: The data describes a typical ribbon cable in the years after 2000. The kind of ribbon cable is produced by international manufacturers and available all over the world. Therefore a global dataset is justifiable.
Technology: The manufacturing process is represented through plastic extrusion (for HDPE and PVC), tin-coating, contouring (brass), and wire drawing (copper).
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: Weighing and measuring of materials. Literature for electricity consumption (assembly), emissions and waste.
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: see Geography and Technology
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_62d03858-9356-3a2c-a739-8f5040b431f8.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
